oindent where $\left|ax_1ightangle$ is dropped from the system for simplicity and $\alpha = {	extstyle{1 \over {\sqrt M }}}$. For a graph $G$ with $n$ vertices and $m$ edges, every edge $(a, b )$ connecting vertcies $a,b \in V$ is associated with a constraint $c_l=v_a\oplus v_b$, where $v_a$ and $v_b$ are the corresponding qubits for vertices $a$ and $b$ in $\left|\Psi_4ightangle$ respectively such that $0 \le l < m$, $0 \le m \le {	extstyle{{n(n - 1)} \over 2}}$, $0 \le a,b \le n-1$ and $a 
e b$, where ${	extstyle{{n(n - 1)} \over 2}}$ is the maximum number of edges in a graph with $n$ vertices. To evaluate the $m$ constraints associated with the edges, add $m$ qubits initialized to state $\left|0ightangle$,  egin{equation}  egin{array}{l} \left|\Psi_5ightangle = \left|\Psi_4ightangle \otimes \left|0ightangle^{\otimes m}\ \,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,\,=\alpha \sum\limits_{k = 0}^{M - 1} { {\left| x_k ightangle \otimes \left|0 ightangle^{\otimes m} } }.\ \end{array} \end{equation} For every constraint $c_l=v_a \oplus v_b$, apply two $Cont\_\sigma_X$ gates, $Cont\_\sigma_X(v_a,c_l)$ and $Cont\_\sigma_X(v_b,c_l)$, so that $\left|c_lightangle=\left|v_a\oplus v_bightangle$. The collection of all $Cont\_\sigma_X$ gates applied to evaluate the $m$ constraints is denoted $C_v$ in Figure ef{alg}, then the system is transformed to,  egin{equation} \left| {\Psi _6 } ightangle = \alpha \sum\limits_{k = 0}^{M - 1} {\left( {\left| x_k ightangle \otimes \left| {c_0^k c_1^k \ldots c_{m-1}^k } ightangle } ight)}, \end{equation} 
oindent where $\sigma _X$ is the Pauli-X gate which is the quantum equivalent to the NOT gate. It can be seen as a rotation of the Bloch Sphere around the X-axis by $\pi$ radians as follows,  egin{equation} \sigma _X = \left[ { egin{array}{*{20}c} 0 & 1 \ 1 & 0 \ \end{array}} ight], \end{equation} and $Cont\_U(v,c)$ gate is a controlled gate with control qubit $\left|vightangle$ and target qubit $\left|cightangle$ that applies a single qubit unitary operator $U$ on $\left|cightangle$ only if $\left|vightangle=\left|1ightangle$, so every qubit $\left|c_l^kightangle$ carries a value of the constraint $c_l$ based on the values of $v_a$ and $v_b$ in the balanced assignment $\left| x_k ightangle$, i.e. the values of $v_a^k$ and $v_b^k$ respectively. Let $\left| z_k ightangle=\left|{c_0^k c_1^k \ldots c_{m-1}^k }ightangle$, then the system can be re-written as follows,  egin{equation} \left| {\Psi _6 } ightangle = \alpha \sum\limits_{k = 0}^{M - 1} {\left( {\left| x_k ightangle \otimes \left| {z_k} ightangle } ight)}, \end{equation} 
oindent where every $\left| x_k ightangle$ is entangled with the corresponding $\left| z_k ightangle$.
